7 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426950 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426967 1069 "q-43593" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426967 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426967 1071 "![](images/f3/f39968d7912eb85cc85354d119565ba8225c5d2fe54dbda029cd99d67e0765e5.png)\n\nA point $B$ is shown on the axes above. To which quadrant does it belong?" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426967 1072 #uuid "17973190-6a31-5b4a-854e-14acb52dfa7f" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426967 1074 "We label the quadrants as follows:\n\n![](images/77/77a74e78ea9c1d880083eb9868d42d547549af73395003ecab4c08d96ce75fe7.png)\n\nSince $B$ is placed above and to the left of the origin, it lies in quadrant $\\text{II},$ which is the second quadrant." 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426968 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426964 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426968 1069 "q-5748" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426968 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426968 1071 "![](images/13/130150cf591ee147d98cc2c265ce1c4790d9570af2b99c0c31d66d9cb7df9b4f.png)\n\nWhat are the $xy$-coordinates of the point shown in the axes above?" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426968 1072 #uuid "1b82d2ba-bd69-538e-a621-832dd1619684" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426968 1074 "To find the coordinates of the point, we inspect its position along the $x$ and $y$ axes.\n\nThe point lies *on* the $y$-axis, $9$ units *below* the origin in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis. So, the point has an $x$-coordinate of $0,$ and a $y$-coordinate of $-9.$\n\nTherefore, its coordinates are $(0,-9).$" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426969 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426959 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426969 1069 "q-22349" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426969 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426969 1071 "Which of the following shows the point $A(-3,4)?$" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426969 1072 #uuid "22c2c4da-83e3-5354-8e45-5160f1d5290b" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426969 1074 "Starting at the origin, we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $A.$\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $A$ has an $x$-coordinate of $-3,$ so we move $3$ units to the *left*, in the *negative* direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $A$ has a $y$-coordinate of $4,$ so we move $4$ units *up*, in the *positive* direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](images/d5/d5143459ae5b0e9704d8faa67dd3acf429832b668eae21ef9ca9e031e551432f.png)" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426970 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426949 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426970 1069 "q-5752" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426970 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426970 1071 "![](images/fe/fe8c79d8a237eab897b0ceea7ab4d4cf9a907360660c223d7486f8e3c5a18958.png)\n\nWhat are the $xy$-coordinates of the point shown in the axes above?" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426970 1072 #uuid "2b4a8301-d80d-5d6b-b666-4d13d2e8333a" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426970 1074 "To find the coordinates of the point, we inspect its position along the $x$ and $y$ axes.\n\nThe point lies *on* the $y$-axis, $1$ unit *below* the origin in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis. So, the point has an $x$-coordinate of $0,$ and a $y$-coordinate of $-1.$\n\nTherefore, its coordinates are $(0,-1).$" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426971 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426960 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426971 1069 "q-61325" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426971 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426971 1071 "![](images/10/10226291288116b0a91ba58fc8d1ee89390965473f914064ee1b6fc386ca04f9.png)\n\nWhat is the $x$-coordinate of the point $P?$" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426971 1072 #uuid "2bac3c45-54bb-59ba-8dfb-2413c5a3c82b" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426971 1074 "To find the coordinates of $P,$ we start at the origin, move $2$ units *right*, and then $4$ units *up*. \n\n![](images/e2/e239fc0e990a133f43f77c608a731f23b5afde0e76950480980be368c616f1c1.png)\n\nThe coordinates of $P$ are $(2,4).$ Therefore, the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is $2.$" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426972 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426956 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426972 1069 "q-61331" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426972 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426972 1071 "Which of the following graphs shows the point $C$ with coordinates $(-3,-1)?$" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426972 1072 #uuid "339cbd4e-71c4-56d8-aa53-97c486b5d7b0" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426972 1074 "To plot a point with coordinates $(-3,-1),$ we start at the origin, move $3$ units left, and then $1$ unit down. \n\n![](images/9e/9ed70a2f54c40a9d9c8879f5dc8a3114db66b5b0bfb6e497fc0ec8c7a9aac92c.png)\n\nSo the correct diagram is:\n\n![](images/a8/a87038ed9828e07b0de813c728bf241fb06cde82ecbbb528e5a3f29c972b4e3b.png)" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426973 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426948 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426973 1069 "q-12470" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426973 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426973 1071 "![](images/d0/d0785d11a903993b04ee55c7fc23f8f219280a45b66df759cbadc1d42fc8c418.png)\n\nWhat are the $xy$-coordinates of the point shown in the axes above?" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426973 1072 #uuid "373c04e2-db02-5c16-a78f-083cd4605e08" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426973 1074 "To find the coordinates of the point, we inspect its position along the $x$ and $y$ axes.\n\nThe point is $2$ units to the right of the origin, in the positive direction of the $x$-axis. So, the point has an $x$-coordinate of $2.$\n\nAdditionally, the point is $4$ units above the origin, in the positive direction of the $y$-axis. So, the point has a $y$-coordinate of $4.$\n\nThe point has an $x$-coordinate of $2$ and a $y$-coordinate of $4,$ so its coordinates are $(2,4).$" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426974 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426952 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426974 1069 "q-109032" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426974 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426974 1071 "![](images/69/697a2ef3438aaea021f0886e1172019744c643acc4195daf126e6f64d0a77917.png)\n\nA point $T$ is shown on the axis above. To which quadrant does it belong?" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426974 1072 #uuid "7df69925-7109-5250-8a7b-f9894f0d9138" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426974 1074 "We label the quadrants as follows:\n\n![](images/41/41a419063ce1bc160023de139406c6ed8f66ab4f7046f223386fc5d93dd60292.png)\n\nSince $T$ is placed below and to the right of the origin, it lies in quadrant $\\text{IV},$ which is the fourth quadrant." 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426975 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426955 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426975 1069 "q-169184" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426975 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426975 1071 "![](images/92/928b00ea1ac59e758c4bc9e224d2d27e1c2149e31d0c5c3ab7673ee9abeae208.png)\n\nWhich of the following is true regarding the point $S?$\n\nI. It is in the fourth quadrant\n\nII. Its $x$-coordinate is $1$\n\nIII. Its $y$-coordinate is $-3$" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426975 1072 #uuid "9298397c-357d-5783-87f8-a9a66297312a" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426975 1074 "The point $S$ is in the third quadrant, so statement I is false.\n\nTo find the coordinates of the point $S,$ we start at the origin, move $1$ units *left*, and then $3$ units *down*. \n\n![](images/f1/f150eac73755dc5f39b499b6ca0ba12624e4c27dd79e7207e11f6c88d04b596d.png)\n\nThe coordinates of $P$ are $(-1,-3).$ Hence, statement II is false and statement III is true." 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426976 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426963 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426976 1069 "q-61352" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426976 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426976 1071 "![](images/ef/efb51633cb6a4bc68d0a7c78ec435cd6a11ce87073e3eb704720c09d75b8b488.png)\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point $B?$" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426976 1072 #uuid "96d78126-7457-56c7-8793-6786c43a01bb" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426976 1074 "To find the coordinates of the point $B,$ we start at the origin, move $3$ unit *left* and then $1$ unit *down*. \n\n![](images/be/be37259f84b49b4ad87e19f8908b7992e9d89e3f51fe96ac36edb5f7220fc694.png)\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of $B$ is $-3,$ the $y$-coordinate is $-1,$ and coordinates are given by the ordered pair $(-3,-1).$" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426977 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426953 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426977 1069 "q-61349" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426977 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426977 1071 "![](images/09/098579a792cd5fe253661082b3cc0a909c68e21a7b6ab11eae4f5a0644cb1195.png)\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point $A?$" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426977 1072 #uuid "becd9473-0ed4-5726-bb5b-2671f06103f1" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426977 1074 "To find the coordinates of the point $A,$ we start at the origin, move $2$ unit *left* and then $3$ units *down*. \n\n![](images/28/28f80206ef851fe3228ca616beb78f5df28d8d1c866cc77f8042af2c8b72e779.png)\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of $A$ is $-2,$ the $y$-coordinate is $-3,$ and coordinates are given by the ordered pair $(-2,-3).$" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426978 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426962 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426978 1069 "q-93506" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426978 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426978 1071 "![](images/15/15dad2803359d456700e8c7788a9d1e5dc956d6410f9ad1e9428fb04ba0013b4.png)\n\nWhat is the $y$-coordinate of the point $Q?$" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426978 1072 #uuid "dd34f23b-b976-5fc4-96ef-147e2f03d920" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426978 1074 "To find the coordinates of $Q,$ we start at the origin, move $2$ units *right*, and then $3$ units *up*. \n\n![](images/c1/c1f81e80803fbbeb12d439ad80a9e146f5db53cd37005984ba7a49f725fce035.png)\n\nThe coordinates of $Q$ are $(2,3).$ Therefore, the $y$-coordinate of $Q$ is $3.$" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426979 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426957 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426979 1069 "q-71672" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426979 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426979 1071 "Which of the following shows the point $A(3,-4)?$" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426979 1072 #uuid "f67f03a1-109e-59a7-989e-ce78b755c960" 13194139534593 17592186045417 true] [17592186426979 1074 "Starting at the origin, we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $A.$\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $A$ has an $x$-coordinate of $3,$ so we move $3$ units to the *right*, in the *positive* direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $A$ has a $y$-coordinate of $-4,$ so we move $4$ units *down*, in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](images/d9/d98351134079c9ccf3b467b6b57df892b0e4ecc6040e32f764f3f9eb4e24989b.png)" 131